 "title": "ADG419: LC2MOS precision SPDT analog switch, 44 V, in 8-lead DIP, cerdip, SOIC and µSOIC",
 "source": {
  "revision": "Rev. A, 1998",
  "pages": 8
 },
 "summary": "A single CMOS SPDT analog switch: IN picks whether D connects to S1 or S2, with break-before-make action. Signals pass both ways and may swing from VSS to VDD, the supplies spanning up to 44 V; it is specified on ±15 V and on a single +12 V. On resistance is 25 Ω typical on ±15 V, leakage sub-nanoamp at room temperature and supply current near zero. It is a pin-for-pin replacement for the DG419.",
